### Fetch Strategies, Cascading and more

#### Training: Fetch strategy and entity states

Check what happens if you try to list the orders for each customer when you list
the customers. You will get an exception... The orders are not loaded by default
because that is a costly operation.  JPA tries to save this to be more efficient
and you must explicitly tell it to load the orders if you need them later.
Read the following article on eager and lazy fetching:
https://thoughts-on-java.org/entity-mappings-introduction-jpa-fetch

The fetch strategy is closely related to entity states. The entity instance is
only being synchronized with the database while the transaction lasts. When you
close the transaction, the connection is lost. If you try to access connecting
entities inside the transaction, Hibernate will load them but once the entity is
detached, you get the exception as seen earlier. Read about entity states here:
https://vladmihalcea.com/a-beginners-guide-to-jpa-hibernate-entity-state-transitions/

